          "id": "1773682740292",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773682740299_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### Context\nAssume the role of a procurement category manager tasked with facilitating negotiations and engaging suppliers to place bids for a {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.negotiationType}} negotiation type. The final outcome of the negotiation will be a {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.outcome}} . Your expertise lies in creating negotiations to ensure the acquisition of essential items and services.\n\n### Instructions\nYour goal is to create a concise one paragraph synopsis in 100 words or less, which will invite potential suppliers to submit a bid or proposal for {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.company}} 's project titled {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.title}} . This synopsis should focus on the strategic importance of the project, highlighting the significance of the categories and descriptions listed under {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.itemCategories}} . \n\n### Acceptance Criteria\nEmploy clear, simple, and professional language throughout your synopsis.\nDo not be too verbose, keep the summary to one paragraph and under 100 words.\nMaintain a third-person perspective to ensure neutrality and professionalism, do not say \"as a procurement category manager\", or use language that includes \"we\", \"I\", or \"you\".\nIntegrate the negotiation item categories and descriptions creatively to underscore their relevance, without directly quoting them.\nAvoid explicit mentions of dates, deadlines, or timelines, focusing instead on the negotiation's objectives and expected benefits.\nExclude any sentences that directly introduce the synopsis, as well as any requests for further assistance.\n\n### Formatting Criteria\nMust translate your output to ({{$context.$nodes.GET_USER_SESSION.$output.items[0].Language}}) language. If you use information that is coming as an input you must translate the labels.\nDo not include headers, footers, signatures, salutations, or closings.\nSteer clear of enumerating item categories or describing them in a list format; instead, weave them into the synopsis smoothly.\nEnsure your synopsis weaves together the negotiation details in a coherent and strategic manner."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Get User Session",
            "toolCode": "ORA_USER_SESSION_TOOL"
          },
          "outcomes": {
